{"title":"2007 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<hr />\n<p>Real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/395ae9da509f9922d790f242adeab5defdc036c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots , a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" /> are given. For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3c0e0875b8695a1e1e2bb48d8c5e73c4e5245f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />) define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/1/661c06518e6a3ae8ca5c84d0eb4e63ef7945723e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_i=\\max\\{a_j:1\\le j\\le i\\}-\\min\\{a_j:i\\le j\\le n\\}\\]\" width=\"370\" height=\"19\" />\nand let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fdac5d8e48dee8050356fb677ae0d7abdbdb118b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d=\\max\\{d_i:1\\le i\\le n\\}.\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(a) Prove that, for any real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/71825596af68ec451a3f19a994f80bc3703769f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1\\le x_2\\le \\cdots\\le x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/0974ea567d7bf6460643f8122d75533897d52d3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\max\\{|x_i-a_i|:1\\le i\\le n\\}\\ge \\dfrac{d}{2}   \\qquad (*)\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>(b) Show that there are real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787ef0f4ea06652fa96f55ccf88d7890d33858cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1\\le x_2\\le x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" /> such that equality holds in (*)\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider five points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8859dbfb7a9ec734e16f2a88fb5cf1104eb6a39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c493dd2882ca1eb621281106a4d91bd73e092e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> be a line passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the interior of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and intersects \nline <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose also that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef75a70c8e27e5644c3cedb93824f38f69ecc358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=EG=EC$\" width=\"134\" height=\"12\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1fc15d59287d2ff7bf581a84f348b3207a0c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a mathematical competition some competitors are friends. Friendship is always mutual. Call a group of competitors a clique if each two of them are friends. (In particular, any group of fewer than two competitors is a clique.) The number of members of a clique is called its size. Given that, in this competition, the largest size of a clique is even, prove that the competitors can be arranged in two rooms such that the largest size of a clique contained in one room is the same as the largest size of a clique contained in the other room.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4cce91d7495d5cfacb65c763159d2bcb63050e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BCA}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> intersects the circumcircle again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. The midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c8afa52afe21f8134664079ca64835b12952dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RPK$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe8ba077ac2e080dc694dd061ebc613ce8c7511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RQL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> have the same area.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Kevin Buzzard and Edward Crane, United Kingdom</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers.  Show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60ffe33c6a761319599d4dd52e41de142e8da64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4ab-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c96ed932b34322b755fd71e93a4476ca2a541e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a^2-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer. Consider\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093e2981f00291b1f43718a1442f9967e2df0a27.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=\\{(x,y,z)~:~x,y,z\\in \\{0,1,\\ldots,n \\},~x+y+z&gt;0\\}\\]\" width=\"422\" height=\"18\" />\nas a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da31929a0cc65a430fe22796e0b8af5da117e17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)^3-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"19\" /> points in three-dimensional space. \nDetermine the smallest possible number of planes, the union of which contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> but does not include <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9f36b13a11a14accae8e072c0cf34d69267bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO\" title=\"2007 IMO\">2007 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems\">2006 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems\">2008 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017165810\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 258/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 854/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 74/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7805/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.570      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.570      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8614:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017165810 and revision id 133461. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}